🛡️ Nmap — SOC Analyst ke liye kya hai?
Nmap = Network Mapper
WORK- Network par kaunse hosts/devices available hain, unke kaunse ports open hain, aur un ports par kya services chal rahi hain — ye discover karna.

1. Nmap actually kya discover karta hai?

📌Suppose company ke network mein:
192.168.1.10   → Windows PC
192.168.1.20   → Linux Server
192.168.1.30   → Web Server
192.168.1.40   → Database Server

📌SOC analyst ko pata lagana hai:
Kaun alive hai?
        ↓
Kaunse ports open hain?
        ↓
Kaunsi service chal rahi hai?
        ↓
Kaunsa version?
        ↓
Kya unexpected exposure hai?

Nmap isi visibility ko provide karta hai.


💡2. Sabse basic scan
nmap 192.168.1.10

Example:
PORT     STATE SERVICE
22/tcp   open  ssh
80/tcp   open  http
443/tcp  open  https

📌Meaning:
Port	     Service	  SOC meaning

22	        SSH	    Remote administration
80	        HTTP	    Web service
443	        HTTPS       Secure web service
3389	        RDP	    Windows remote access
445	        SMB	    Windows file sharing
53              DNS	    DNS service
25	        SMTP	    Mail service

Important: Open port automatically = vulnerability nahi.


💎Common Commands
Command	What it does	                      When to use	                                        Risk

nmap 192.168.1.1                              Basic scan - Scans the 1000 most common ports	        Quick check for open ports	
nmap -sV 192.168.1.1                          Version detection - Identifies service versions        	Know what software is running	
nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24	                      Ping scan - Find live hosts without port scan	        Discover hosts on network	
nmap -p 80,443 192.168.1.1                    Specific ports - Scan only specified ports	        Target specific services	
nmap -sS 192.168.1.1                          SYN Stealth scan - Half-open, faster, less detectable	Stealthy scanning	
nmap -sT 192.168.1.1	                      TCP Connect scan - Full TCP handshake	                When SYN scan not available	
nmap -sU 192.168.1.1	                      UDP scan - Scan UDP ports	                                Find UDP services like DNS, SNMP	
nmap -p- 192.168.1.1	                      Full port scan - All 65535 ports	                        Complete port enumeration	
nmap -O 192.168.1.1                           OS detection - Identify operating system	                Know target OS	
nmap -A 192.168.1.1                           Aggressive scan - OS, version, scripts, traceroute	Comprehensive info gathering	
nmap -sS -sV -O -p- -T4 192.168.1.1           Full enumeration - Stealth + version + OS + all ports	Complete target profile	
nmap --script vuln 192.168.1.1	              Vulnerability scan - Run vuln detection scripts	        Find known vulnerabilities	
nmap --script=http-enum 192.168.1.1	      HTTP enumeration - Find web directories	                Web server recon	
nmap --script=smb-vuln* 192.168.1.1	      SMB vulnerability scan - Check SMB vulns                	Windows SMB testing	
nmap -sV --script=banner 192.168.1.1	      Banner grabbing - Get service banners                	Identify services	
nmap -sS -Pn -n --disable-arp-ping 192.168.1.1	Firewall bypass - Skip host discovery                	When ICMP blocked	
nmap -sS -f 192.168.1.1                        Fragment packets - Evade simple firewalls        	IDS/Firewall evasion	
nmap -D RND:10 192.168.1.1                     Decoy scan - Use random decoy IPs	                Hide real IP	
nmap --source-port 53 192.168.1.1              Source port spoof - Use trusted port	                Bypass port-based firewall	
nmap -sI zombie_ip 192.168.1.1	               Idle/Zombie scan - Completely anonymous	                Ultimate stealth	
nmap --script=default,safe 192.168.1.1         Safe scripts - Run non-intrusive scripts	                Safe enumeration	
nmap -oA scan_results 192.168.1.1	       Save all formats - Output to all file types        	Documentation	
nmap -iL targets.txt -oN output.txt	       Batch scan - Scan from file, save results	        Multiple targets	
nmap --script "http-* and not http-brute" 192.168.1.1Script filter - Run specific script categories	Targeted enumeration	


















